### 3️⃣ Environment variables you must set for a **pure self‑hosted core**  

| Variable | Required? | What it does |
|----------|-----------|--------------|
| `DATABASE_URL` | ✅ | Prisma DB connection (PostgreSQL, SQLite, MySQL – whatever you prefer). |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | ✅ | Base URL used when the server builds URLs for digests, QStash callbacks, etc. |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` | ✅ (if you’ll use Gmail) | OAuth client for Google. |
| `OUTLOOK_CLIENT_ID / OUTLOOK_CLIENT_SECRET` | ✅ (if you’ll use Outlook) | OAuth client for Microsoft Graph. |
| `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` (or whichever auth lib you use) | ✅ | Session signing. |
| `RESEND_FROM_EMAIL` | **optional** (only if you keep Resend) | “From” address for digests. |
| `POSTHOG_API_KEY` | **optional** | If you keep analytics. |
| `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | **optional** | If you keep Stripe. |
| `QSTASH_TOKEN`, `QSTASH_URL` | **optional** | If you keep QStash. |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `CLAUDE_API_KEY` | **optional** | If you keep AI features. |

> **Tip:** For a *minimal* installation you can set the optional vars to empty strings or omit them entirely. The code paths that depend on them will simply short‑circuit (e.g., UI buttons disabled, premium‑only routes return a “not available” error).

